config NEON_MDF_TLS
    bool "Build Neon TLS (mbedTLS 3.6.8 LTS over lwIP sockets)"
    default n
    depends on NEON_MDF_NET
    help
        TLS 1.2 client/server sessions over lwIP sockets with software
        crypto. The application adds it with neon_mdf_add_tls() after
        neon_mdf_add_net(). mbedTLS 3.6 LTS is supported until March 2027.

if NEON_MDF_TLS

config NEON_MDF_TLS_MAX_SESSIONS
    int "TLS sessions that can exist at once"
    default 2
    range 1 8
    help
        Static handle pool. Each live session also takes up to about 48 KiB
        of FreeRTOS heap during an ECDHE handshake (16 KiB input record,
        4 KiB output record, handshake state, certificates).

config NEON_MDF_TLS_DEV_ENTROPY
    bool "Development entropy from timer jitter (INSECURE)"
    default y
    help
        FX1 has no documented TRNG yet. This source mixes mtime jitter and
        the MAC address; on the VP it is fully deterministic. It lets TLS run
        for bring-up only: keys and nonces are predictable. Disable it and
        provide neon_tls_port_entropy() from a real TRNG for any product.

endif
